# EXAMPLE STUB - NOT A REAL PATCH - NOT LISTED IN series
#
# This file is an illustration of the format for a patch that EDITS an existing
# Chromium file, which is what every behavioural patch does. It is deliberately
# named .patch.stub so no tool can pick it up, and kernel/verify-patches.sh
# ignores it because series never names it.
#
# WHY IT IS NOT A REAL PATCH
# The hunks below do not come from a real checkout. The context lines are
# invented, the line numbers are made up, and the blob hashes are zeros, so
# `git apply --check` would reject this on 155.0.8059.85 and on every other tag.
# We do not have a Chromium checkout on the authoring machine, and a diff
# written without one cannot be honest.
#
# WHAT TO DO INSTEAD
# Follow docs/kernel/patch-pipeline.md, "Write a patch on a checkout". Take the
# real file at the pinned tag, edit it there, and generate the diff with
#   diff -u --label a/PATH --label b/PATH orig edited
# which produces correct hunk headers and correct context by construction.
#
# The three parts below - subject, description, headers - are exactly what a
# real patch must carry. Only the diff body is fake.

Subject: [PATCH] blink: example of a context patch against an existing file

Illustrates the shape of a patch that changes a value Chromium already
computes, in this example the reported hardware concurrency. The real patch
would name the surface (hardware_concurrency), say what a page sees
afterwards, and say what stays as in stock Chromium.

Nanfu-Patch-Applies-To: 155.0.8059.85
Nanfu-Patch-Promise: third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_base.cc::kNanfuExample
Nanfu-Patch-Repo: .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERYTHING BELOW THIS LINE IS INVENTED AND WILL NOT APPLY. DO NOT SHIP IT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_base.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_base.cc
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_base.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_base.cc
@@ -1,7 +1,9 @@
 // context lines here are invented, not read from the tree

 unsigned NavigatorBase::hardwareConcurrency() const {
-  return base::SysInfo::NumberOfProcessors();
+  // kNanfuExample: the real patch would read the composed profile here.
+  return profile_hardware_concurrency_or_host();
 }

 // more invented context follows
